comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-23T21:28:11.224Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: all-status searches for Windows plugin npm.cmd, in-process Claude plugin and launcher showed pm-arax closed the earlier extension npm command issue and pm-l9wl closed the copied Claude plugin defect; neither covers this newly generated plugin resolver Windows first-install transport. Reuse pm-z3ez agent-distribution parent and link both historical causes. Review evidence: PR #1292 CodeRabbit inline thread at templates/agent-plugins/plugin-runtime.mjs."
  "2026-09-23T21:28:30.768Z","harness:codex","Node official child_process documentation for current and Node 22 says Windows .cmd/.bat cannot be launched directly; use cmd.exe as a child. The prior pm-arax extension fix already had a review follow-up for the same shell requirement. The plugin resolver remains standalone inside copied marketplace caches, so this repair belongs in its shared generated template and a native Windows regression."
  "2026-09-23T21:31:21.848Z","harness:codex","TDD red: before the resolver change, both Claude and Codex simulated-Windows command tests failed because the default installer received npm.cmd directly instead of cmd.exe. Implemented a fixed npm command string via cmd.exe /d /v:off /s /c with windowsVerbatimArguments and passed the staging root through the child environment; regenerated both plugin copies. Focused resolver tests now pass 28/28 on Linux. Added a native Windows integration test with a real .cmd shim and a staging path containing spaces, ampersand and percent, required in the Windows regression job. Hosted proof pending."
  "2026-09-23T21:36:50.541Z","harness:codex","Local focused PM linked-test run passed 43 assertions; the two real command-processor cases are correctly skipped on Linux and required in Windows CI. pnpm typecheck, pnpm security:scan, pnpm smoke:plugin-cache, and generated-wrapper byte parity pass. The native Windows acceptance still needs hosted execution before closure."
  "2026-09-23T21:47:55.150Z","harness:codex","Hosted PR #1292 run 35923549944 reached the new native Windows transport test. Both Claude and Codex real cmd.exe/npm.cmd shim cases passed with spaces, ampersand and percent in the staging path. The Windows job failed only because the adjacent simulated race test still expected Linux npm on Windows; corrected that expectation. The static gate failed its orphaned-path ceiling because the new integration test was committed before its PM file link; this push includes the linked PM item. No product command transport failure was observed."
  "2026-09-23T22:03:01.499Z","harness:codex","Hosted acceptance: PR #1292 run 35924635377 at dcbd12fd7c47fdc51d13335a50117f811d01c9fe passed Windows regression, static, exact coverage, smokes and all required checks. The new real Windows command-processor integration ran both Claude and Codex cases with a staging path containing spaces, ampersand and percent; the corrected Windows race assertions passed. Earlier run 35923549944 had already passed the two real transport cases but failed the old Linux-only assertion, now fixed. Static orphan negative control is restored by the committed PM file link."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-23T22:03:02.174Z","harness:codex","A Windows npm.cmd shim needs cmd.exe; invoking the .cmd file directly from Node child_process is not portable. Keep the command processor text limited to fixed flags and validated package version, pass caller-controlled paths through the child environment, disable delayed expansion, and run a native Windows transport fixture in a required PR job."
